<!DOCTYPE html><html lang="en"><head><base target="_self"/><meta charSet="utf-8"/><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0"/><meta http-equiv="X-UA-Compatible" content="IE=Edge"/><meta name="google" content="notranslate"/><title data-rh="true">Discrimination Lawsuit Over Workday’s AI Hiring Tools Can Proceed as Class Action: 6 Things Employers Should Do After Latest Court Decision | Fisher Phillips LLP</title><meta name="description" content="A federal judge just allowed a job applicant’s lawsuit against Workday to move forward as a nationwide class action, ruling that the company’s AI-powered hiring tools may have had a discriminatory impact on applicants over age 40. The May 16 decision is a major development in Mobley v. Workday, one of the country’s most closely watched legal challenges to the use of artificial intelligence in employment decisions. While this age discrimination case is still in its early stages, the ruling serves as a warning to employers and AI vendors alike that they can be held accountable for algorithmic screening tools if they disproportionately harm protected groups – even if the bias wasn’t intentional. What do you need to know about last week’s critical ruling?" data-rh="true"/><meta name="keywords" content="Workday lawsuit, Derek Mobley sued Workday, Mobley vs Workday, Mobley v Workday, workday class action lawsuit, workday ai lawsuit, discrimination lawsuit settlement" data-rh="true"/><link rel="canonical" href="https://www.fisherphillips.com/en/insights/insights/discrimination-lawsuit-over-workdays-ai-hiring-tools-can-proceed-as-class-action-6-things"/><link rel="apple-touch-icon" sizes="180x180" href="/images/build/apple-touch-icon_a503a8d8.png"/><link rel="icon" type="image/png" sizes="96x96" href="/images/build/favicon-96x96_4949b69c.png"/><link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/images/build/favicon_03998ed0.svg"/><link rel="manifest" href="/images/build/site_62fbec0b.webmanifest"/><link rel="mask-icon" href="/images/build/favicon_03998ed0.svg" color="#eb002c"/><link rel="shortcut icon" href="/images/build/favicon_11de8639.ico"/><meta name="apple-mobile-web-app-title" content="Fisher Phillips LLP"/><meta name="application-name" content="Fisher Phillips LLP"/><meta name="theme-color" content="#eb002c"/><meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image"/><meta property="og:description" content="A federal judge just allowed a job applicant’s lawsuit against Workday to move forward as a nationwide class action, ruling that the company’s AI-powered hiring tools may have had a discriminatory impact on applicants over age 40. The May 16 decision is a major development in Mobley v. Workday, one of the country’s most closely watched legal challenges to the use of artificial intelligence in employment decisions. While this age discrimination case is still in its early stages, the ruling serves as a warning to employers and AI vendors alike that they can be held accountable for algorithmic screening tools if they disproportionately harm protected groups – even if the bias wasn’t intentional. What do you need to know about last week’s critical ruling?"/><meta property="og:image" content="https://www.fisherphillips.com/a/web/mFybRo4tAuKY5QLPPRkK9j/bj2jze/opengraph.png"/><meta property="og:image:secure_url" content="https://www.fisherphillips.com/a/web/mFybRo4tAuKY5QLPPRkK9j/bj2jze/opengraph.png"/><meta property="og:site_name" content="Fisher Phillips"/><meta property="og:title" content="Discrimination Lawsuit Over Workday’s AI Hiring Tools Can Proceed as Class Action: 6 Things Employers Should Do After Latest Court Decision"/><meta property="og:type" content="website"/><meta property="og:url" content="https://www.fisherphillips.com/en/insights/insights/discrimination-lawsuit-over-workdays-ai-hiring-tools-can-proceed-as-class-action-6-things"/><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"http://schema.org","@graph":[{"@type":"WebPage","@id":"https://www.fisherphillips.com/en/insights/insights/discrimination-lawsuit-over-workdays-ai-hiring-tools-can-proceed-as-class-action-6-things","name":"Discrimination Lawsuit Over Workday’s AI Hiring Tools Can Proceed as Class Action: 6 Things Employers Should Do After Latest Court Decision","url":"https://www.fisherphillips.com/en/insights/insights/discrimination-lawsuit-over-workdays-ai-hiring-tools-can-proceed-as-class-action-6-things","description":"A federal judge just allowed a job applicant’s lawsuit against Workday to move forward as a nationwide class action, ruling that the company’s AI-powered hiring tools may have had a discriminatory impact on applicants over age 40. The May 16 decision is a major development in Mobley v. Workday, one of the country’s most closely watched legal challenges to the use of artificial intelligence in employment decisions. While this age discrimination case is still in its early stages, the ruling serves as a warning to employers and AI vendors alike that they can be held accountable for algorithmic screening tools if they disproportionately harm protected groups – even if the bias wasn’t intentional. What do you need to know about last week’s critical ruling?","image":["https://www.fisherphillips.com/a/web/mFybRo4tAuKY5QLPPRkK9j/bj2jze/opengraph.png"],"mainEntity":{"@id":"https://www.fisherphillips.com/en/insights/insights/discrimination-lawsuit-over-workdays-ai-hiring-tools-can-proceed-as-class-action-6-things#news"},"breadcrumb":{"@id":"https://www.fisherphillips.com/en/insights/insights/discrimination-lawsuit-over-workdays-ai-hiring-tools-can-proceed-as-class-action-6-things#breadcrumbs"}},{"@type":"NewsArticle","@id":"https://www.fisherphillips.com/en/insights/insights/discrimination-lawsuit-over-workdays-ai-hiring-tools-can-proceed-as-class-action-6-things#news","mainEntityOfPage":{"@id":"https://www.fisherphillips.com/en/insights/insights/discrimination-lawsuit-over-workdays-ai-hiring-tools-can-proceed-as-class-action-6-things"},"name":"Discrimination Lawsuit Over Workday’s AI Hiring Tools Can Proceed as Class Action: 6 Things Employers Should Do After Latest Court Decision","headline":"Discrimination Lawsuit Over Workday’s AI Hiring Tools Can Proceed as Class Action: 6 Things Employers Should Do After Latest Court Decision","image":["https://www.fisherphillips.com/a/web/mFybRo4tAuKY5QLPPRkK9j/bj2jze/opengraph.png"],"datePublished":"2025-05-20T00:00:00Z","author":[],"publisher":{"@id":"https://www.fisherphillips.com/en#firm"},"description":"A federal judge just allowed a job applicant’s lawsuit against Workday to move forward as a nationwide class action, ruling that the company’s AI-powered hiring tools may have had a discriminatory impact on applicants over age 40. The May 16 decision is a major development in Mobley v. Workday, one of the country’s most closely watched legal challenges to the use of artificial intelligence in employment decisions. While this age discrimination case is still in its early stages, the ruling serves as a warning to employers and AI vendors alike that they can be held accountable for algorithmic screening tools if they disproportionately harm protected groups – even if the bias wasn’t intentional. What do you need to know about last week’s critical ruling?"},{"@type":"BreadcrumbList","@id":"https://www.fisherphillips.com/en/insights/insights/discrimination-lawsuit-over-workdays-ai-hiring-tools-can-proceed-as-class-action-6-things#breadcrumbs","itemListElement":[{"@type":"ListItem","name":"Fisher Phillips LLP","item":"https://www.fisherphillips.com/en","position":1},{"@type":"ListItem","name":"Insights, News & Events","item":"https://www.fisherphillips.com/en/insights","position":2},{"@type":"ListItem","name":"Insights","item":"https://www.fisherphillips.com/en/insights/insights","position":3},{"@type":"ListItem","name":"Discrimination Lawsuit Over Workday’s AI Hiring Tools Can Proceed as Class Action: 6 Things Employers Should Do After Latest Court Decision","position":4}]}]}</script><link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com"/><link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin="anonymous"/><link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Inter:ital,opsz,wght@0,14..32,100..900;1,14..32,100..900&amp;display=swap" rel="stylesheet"/><link rel="stylesheet" type="text/css" href="/_theming/1/dc0b65040d86b9c1b90094551275158bf78948532e35af6d784bfb817f4627da/theming.css"/><link rel="stylesheet" type="text/css" href="/cached/40018/styles/build/news.css"/><link rel="stylesheet" type="text/css" href="/cached/40018/styles/dist/fontawesome-free-6.4.2-web/css/fontawesome.min.css"/><link rel="stylesheet" type="text/css" href="/cached/40018/styles/dist/fontawesome-free-6.4.2-web/css/brands.min.css"/><link rel="stylesheet" type="text/css" href="/cached/40018/styles/dist/fontawesome-free-6.4.2-web/css/solid.min.css"/><link rel="stylesheet" type="text/css" href="/cached/40018/styles/dist/fontawesome-free-6.4.2-web/css/regular.min.css"/><script>// Designed by DeSantis Breindel - https://www.desantisbreindel.com
